# Git branch workflow (must)

**Default branch for all new work:** `dev`  
**Production / push target after verify:** `main`

## Next time (every change)

1. **Build on `dev`**
   - `git checkout dev` (create from `main` if missing: `git checkout -b dev`)
   - Commit all feature / UI / fix work here
   - Do **not** commit unfinished work straight to `main`

2. **Verify on `dev`**
   - `npm run build` green
   - Spot-check critical UI (hero → footer) + mobile
   - Only then merge

3. **Merge into `main` + push `main`**
   - `git checkout main`
   - `git pull origin main` (if remote exists)
   - `git merge dev` (prefer fast-forward when possible)
   - `git push origin main`
   - Never force-push `main` unless the user explicitly asks

4. **Sync `dev` back up-to-date with `main`**
   - `git checkout dev`
   - `git merge main` (or `git rebase main` only if user asks)
   - `git push origin dev` (so remote `dev` matches)
   - Confirm: `dev` and `main` point at the same commit (or `dev` is not behind `main`)

## Rules

- Day-to-day coding + commits → **`dev`**
- Release / verified ship → merge → **`main`** → push **`main`**
- After every successful main push → bring **`dev`** current again
- Do not leave `dev` stale behind `main`
- Do not open PRs / pushes to `main` with unverified broken builds

## Quick checklist

- [ ] Working on `dev`
- [ ] `npm run build` OK
- [ ] Merged `dev` → `main`
- [ ] Pushed `origin/main`
- [ ] `dev` synced from `main` + pushed if remote exists
